A||||22||Sootah||Need your advice, 88 coupe or 85 SE?||||1||
Z||000000||Sootah||09-08-2001||09:09 PM||||Allrighty fellas, I've been looking at a couple of Fieros. One is a Silver 85 SE 5-speed. Perfect paint and interior. 115,000. Even has a pioneer CD changer! $1500. Other is an '88 coupe. Can't member what color (havent been to see it yet, only talked to the guy) interior is supposedly in good condition, paint OK, 135,000, but its an auto.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Coupled with the 4-banger. Asking price is $1000 but he sounds like he wants to sell pretty bad so I bet I can get it to like $700.<P>I know the Iron Duke isn't the most powerfull engine out there, but my buddy's 85 coupe with 5 speed moves pretty good. I'm worried that this will end up gutless with the auto. I wanna fast car and frankly, the auto scares the hell out of me. I want to avoid one at all costs.<P><P>------------------<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haagster||09-08-2001||09:46 PM||||Then you answered your own question.  There are a few benefits of an 88 over an 85, but if you DON'T want an automatic, you will never be happy with it (unless you swap engines/transmission/etc etc etc).  By the time you pay for all of that, you would have been farther ahead just to get what you wanted in the first place.<P>I've been there.  I had an 88 coupe (automatic) for 6 years.   It ran fine for me, but I wanted to get into a V6, so I traded it for an 87GT last June.  GL<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Haagster (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||fiero_hunter85||09-08-2001||10:43 PM||||i used to have a 88 fiero coupe with an auto tranni and i can tell you they ARE gutless. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sootah||09-08-2001||10:47 PM||||I think I'll see if I can get it for $500, if not then I will pass.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||09-08-2001||11:47 PM||||If I remember correctly, this will be your first Fiero.....right?  If that is the case, go with the '88 auto.  You will have far fewer driveability issues with the auto. than the 5-sp.   You can almost bet that the clutch on the '85 is going or will soon go and repairs will almost equal what you paid for the thing.<P>Also, the '88 will have a better resale value, or at least will be easier to sell when the "right" one comes along at a later date.  <P>Do yourself a favor and get the '88, get the "feel" for Fieros and then look for one with a stick and/or V-6 at a later date (once you're more comfortable with the Fiero in general).<P>This is just my opinion, but I don't want to read another "My car sucks" or "I'm gonna chuck my Fiero off of a cliff" type of post when your clutch fails or you have some other catastrophic failure with the '85.<P>Another factor is the engines themselves......the '88 Duke is a much better motor than the '85 Duke (smoother, more reliable, etc.).  I'd buy the '88 for no other reason. <P>I owned an '87 auto. coupe with an '88 engine and while it was short on all out performance, it wasn't that much of a "dog".  <P>Enough rambling......you have my vote for the '88.<P>Good luck!<P><BR>BTW.....if you do pass on the '88 give me the sellers info.  I might just buy it for a winter beater!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroMaster88||09-09-2001||12:18 AM||||I say go with the 88...drive it for a while then do what i did..put the V6 5 speed in it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sootah||09-09-2001||01:37 AM||||Actually the '85 just had the clutch replaced. It's also a lot closer. I really don't know what I am leaning twoard more now. With the '88 I do have the forum on my side when it comes selling time for it, so hopefully it will go easily. I'll make my friend take me to see it tommorow. If I can't get him to do it I will have to wait till the 21'st to go look at it (payday), as well as a few others that are in that area.<P>Thanx 4 the replies. Keep em coming. Oh, and is there a place where I can get the 0-60 time for the '88 coupe? I'd at least like to know about what I will be doing.<P>-<B>Sootah</B><P>------------------<BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||09-09-2001||01:50 AM||||A very un-scientific 0-60 time is about 10 seconds.<BR>Actually, I turned a corner and stomped it, at the same time I looked at my watch. Was at 60 about 10 seconds later. <BR>Like I said... very un-scientific. But you get the idea.<P>I'd say go with the 88. If it's in any kind of decent shape, you can always get your money out of it.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Sootah||09-09-2001||03:09 AM||||Assuming I get the '88, buff it, make the interior look nice, add a CD player, etc. How much do you think I could get out of it when I go to sell it? (Assuming I do, I may just totally fall in love with it and try to elope. Hawaii is pretty lax about what you can marry...)<P>Insert 2¢ now. Thank you and have a nice day.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||09-09-2001||10:36 AM||||Not sure, but I think I've seen non-running 88s go for a grand.<BR>I paid $2K for an 88 with 114,000 miles on it, but it was *spotless*.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Master_Sushi||09-10-2001||08:05 AM||||If your on a budget get the 88. But if you want good 0-60 times (good duke times) get the 85. I have an 88 coupe auto, I can hit 0-60 in like 9 secs. I have almost no mods. I`m going to get a G-Tech and time it  one day. You will like the handeling of the 88 over the 85 assuming both are in good shape. Also it is a 3 year newer car. Also, I think the 88 coupe's look way better then 85se's. No bumper pads, better interiour, the engine is DIS, few other little improvements. Only bad part about an 88 are getting parts, suspention parts can be more, as can brakes. But with people on the forum its not a big deal.<BR>Anyway... Let us know what you decide on getting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>88 Fiero Coupe...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mesopotamis_1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000011||Master_Sushi||09-10-2001||08:09 AM||||Things I forgot to add in my post...<BR>The 88's have better brakes, less problumed headlights, I beleave the engines in the 88/87's did make a bit more HP also.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Springtyme||09-10-2001||08:39 AM||||My first Fiero is is an 88 coupe and I love it to death. Eventually I'll get more =) But I wouldn't trade it in for the world. I love the suspension on it. Being able to take highway entrance ramps at 60 mph feels like you're flying =)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> <P>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||4
Z||000013||Springtyme||09-10-2001||08:46 AM||||Hay master Sushi, my car looks like yours =)<P>I paid $1,700 for my 88 coupe, interior spotless and only 72k miles on it, but the woman didn't know what she had. When we went to the Notary, they asked why she was selling it so much lower than the book value, cause it's worth about 3,400 the way it stands now. =) In other words, if I was strapped for cash and needed a quick fix, I could sell it and get double what I paid for it.<P>Also, The V6's aren't that much faster. My boyfriend has one and I kicked his @$$ on the highway. Once I took off, all I saw was him in my rearview. I also lost him on back windy roads, but if you're looking to race stop light to stop light, forget it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg">  <P>            ~Springtyme~<p>[This message has been edited by Springtyme (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||ChadMan||09-10-2001||09:05 AM||||I love my 88 Coupe...but I'm going to have to advise you to get the 85 SE.<P>My 88 has been very reliable, but as the miles have piled up and parts have worn out such as brake calipers, shocks/struts, ball joints, tie rod ends, etc, I have found that a lot of the parts that were unique to the 88 are getting harder to find and more expensive.<P>Instead of paying $80/side for rear brake calipers for the 85 and walking out of Autozone with them that day, you'll be paying $140/side and waiting a week for them to arrive from the Fiero Store.<P>Also, the automatic seems to bog down the Duke much more than it does the V6 (putting flame suit on).||||reg||1
Z||000015||Formula||09-10-2001||09:11 AM||||I started with an 88 Formula-auto, and it has some power. (V6, auto) Next summer its getting a 5 -speed to go with the stroker though.<P>I've never driven, or been in a 4 cyl fiero so idk what to tell you, but 88 suspensions rock! (put the gt/formula sway bars on it though)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/StrokeThis.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Master_Sushi||09-10-2001||12:25 PM||||Hey springtyme,<BR>Ya I noticed your car is almost identical to mine     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I paid 2600 for mine about 2 years ago now. It had 45k miles at the time, in mint shape. Owned by an older lady. So I was sold when I saw it     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. All the options mine has are.. AC,Auto,Rear Defrost,luggage rack. I also added a sunroof, upgraded stereo, and a few other misc things. What options does yours have? Be interesting to see if they are identical, or had the same option package or something.<P>Heres when I first got it...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Oldfiero.jpg">  <P><B>88 Coupes are the best!</B><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
